@flexiarg cascade-construction/run-it-on-a-real-case
@title Run The Constructed Cascade On A Real Recorded Case Before Building Anything
@keywords evaluation, recorded-state, counterfactual, saving, retarget, construction
@audience agents constructing cascades, owners deciding what to build
@tone technical
@style pattern
@status draft 2026-09-17 (claude-7; three runs on 2026-09-16)
@execution deterministic given the recorded state and the interpretation; its value is mostly epistemic. Reading q0 from the record may need LLM judgement.
@epistemic-value the main epistemic move. It observes whether the cascade reproduces recorded behaviour, and each disagreement resolves an interpretation or names an implementation defect.
@done done after one recorded case per distinct outcome the cascade predicts (for example enabled vs blocked act), or when no recorded case exists, which is recorded. A further case is run only if it could change a guard, a grain or the decision.
@references [pattern-interpretation/reproduce-the-recorded-run translation/test-by-reproducing-behaviour cascade-construction/read-what-exists-first]
@see-also apparatus/monitors-measure-the-work
@why a constructed cascade is a hypothesis about what a system should do. Running it on one real case from recorded state costs little and says whether it reproduces what happened, whether the implementation diverges from it, and — for a feature not yet built — how much the feature would actually change.
@how take a recorded case (a state packet, a gate run, a reviewed delivery); read q0 from it with sources; run the cascade; compare with what happened; for an unbuilt feature, also run the counterfactual with the feature in place and measure the difference on the case. Let the result change the design before any code is commissioned.
@violation-signature a feature built on an assumed saving; a cascade presented without ever meeting a real state; a divergence from the implementation explained away rather than recorded.
! conclusion: Run a new cascade on a real recorded case, and for unbuilt features on its counterfactual, and let the result reshape the design before building.

  + context: A cascade has been constructed and a build is being considered.

  + IF:
    A real recorded case of the problem exists.

  + HOWEVER:
    The design already looks right, and running it takes an hour.

  + THEN:
    Run it, compare, and measure the counterfactual difference.

  + BECAUSE:
    The case shows reproduction, implementation divergence and actual benefit, none of which reading the cascade shows.

  + evidence: buffer cleaner reproduced "no threshold-eligible wiring"; inbox zero diverged from the implementation and named three defects (futon0 027b55e); test registry on futon2 cb5f8b1288 would have saved 2 of 64 deftests, which moved the proposed first target to repeated verification of unchanged content by successive agents (finding F9).
